        <body>
            <div xml:id="d692">

                <pb facs="1401" n="1361" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p1/pg1361"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">684A.85/10–1753: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 692<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Egypt (Caffery) to the Department of State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d692-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-10-17T15:00:00+02:00">October 17, 1953—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>466. Paris for Johnston. Minister Foreign
                    Affairs assured me this morning re recent Israeli attacks on Jordan villages
                    excitement is rising high in Arab world. Egypt is trying “to hold back” and “not
                    stir up trouble” and even to avoid having these incidents brought before
                    Security Council. In other words Egypt is trying to exert a calming influence.
                    However, Egyptian Government is very much concerned about possibility that
                    Israeli Government has “much bigger things in mind. Recent tendencies are not
                    good”, e. g., (1) <pb facs="1402" n="1362" xml:id="pg1362"/> Jordan waters (2)
                    Huleh swamps (3) El Auja (4) other recent attacks across the frontier including
                    Gaza district.</p>
                <p>He went on to say that during last Arab League Council meeting here Jordan
                    Government emphasized fear of Israeli attacks against Jordan frontier villages.
                    They asked for help. Only help other Arab countries gave was subsidy of half
                    million dinars for economic subsidies to frontier villages. (In some villages
                    inhabitants are “starving” because they cannot cultivate their ex-properties
                    across the frontier.)</p>
                <p>He indicated that whole Arab world is anxiously awaiting Washington reaction.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d692-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d692-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to London, Paris, Jerusalem, Beirut, Damascus, Baghdad, Amman, Jidda,
                    and Tel Aviv.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
